{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 8, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a prince of the Crusader state of Tripoli. He was born around 1140 and was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *Early Life* Raymond III was still a child when his father was assassinated in 1152 and he succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. His mother Hodierna acted as regent for him until he came of age. Raymond III was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi in 1164 during the Battle of Harim and was held prisoner for about 10 years. During his captivity his stepbrother Bohemond III of Antioch acted as regent.\n\n*Reign* After his release from captivity Raymond III returned to Tripoli and took control of his county. He was determined to avenge his long captivity and launched several attacks against Nur ad-Din's successors. Raymond III was also involved in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and played a significant role in the events leading up to the Battle of Hattin. He was a cousin of King Baldwin IV and was one of the few nobles who remained loyal to him. Raymond III was also a strong supporter of the leper king and opposed the influence of Guy of Lusignan.\n\n*Succession and Legacy* Raymond III died in 1187 without an heir and his county was inherited by his godson Raymond IV of Antioch. Raymond III's legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a skilled military leader and a shrewd politician who played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states. His reign was marked by both military successes and failures and he was often at odds with his neighbors and rivals. Despite his many challenges Raymond III remained a committed defender of his county and his faith until the end of his life. He was a key figure in the events leading up to the Battle of Hattin and his actions had significant consequences for the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Crusader states as a whole. Raymond III's life and reign are a testament to the complexities and challenges of the Crusader period.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.018178174272179604}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.00020382710499688983}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0016012478154152632}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.25561580061912537}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.02954106591641903}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.6682023406028748}, {"token": " prince", "logprob": -2.2162938117980957}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.039226751774549484}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.009085266850888729}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -0.47412991523742676}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0010944573441520333}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.31341275572776794}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.0005645350320264697}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.00038092033355496824}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0002227773511549458}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.0392531156539917}, {"token": " around", "logprob": -0.6931648254394531}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0009121309849433601}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1395233869552612}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.7179348762729205e-05}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -2.2172682292875834e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.0004659997357521206}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -7.033323527139146e-06}, {"token": " o